      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the code. The key improvements I'll make:\n1. Remove ~50 unused imports (ChronoField, time-of-day fields, etc.) not needed by this test\n2. Remove unused class-level constants (`MAX_LENGTH`, `TEST`, `PARIS`)\n3. Remove unrelated `test_now`/`test_now_ZoneId` helper tests that belong to the main test suite, not this focused class\n4. Add a brief comment explaining *why* day 28 is meaningful (valid for every month, including February)The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version strips ~60 unused imports, removes three unused class-level constants, drops the two unrelated `test_now` helper methods, renames the local variable to `day28` for clarity, and adds a Javadoc comment explaining why day 28 is the meaningful boundary case (the highest day valid in all 12 months, so no clamping occurs)."
    }
